---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ContentLayout from "../components/ContentLayout.astro";
import { site } from "../config/site";

const { availability } = site;
---

<BaseLayout>
  <main id="main-content" class="page-main shell">
    <ContentLayout>
      <div class="home-content">
        <section class="home-hero">
          <h1>{site.name}</h1>
          <p class="hero__lead">
            I am a PhD student in Electrical and Computer Engineering at Purdue University and a Graduate Research
            Assistant in the <a href="https://davisjam.github.io/research/">Duality Lab</a>, advised by James C. Davis.
          </p>
          <p class="hero__lead">
            I build methods and tools that give rigorous guarantees about software correctness: formal verification,
            program analysis, and automated testing applied at industrial scale. AutoSOUP, which automates
            memory-safety verification of C components, is accepted at <a href="/publication/autosoup/">ACM CCS 2026</a>.
            My work on reducing false positives in Google's OSS-Fuzz-Gen appears at <a href="/publication/lessons-oss-fuzz-gen/">FSE 2026</a>,
            and EmNetTest found seven previously unknown defects, six of them assigned CVEs, in widely used embedded
            network stacks.
          </p>
          <p class="hero-interests">
            <span class="hero-interests__label">Research interests</span>
            Formal verification · Program analysis and testing · Performance optimization
          </p>
          {availability.seeking && (
            <p class="hero-availability">Seeking {availability.term} {availability.kind}</p>
          )}
          <div class="hero-actions">
            <a class="button-link" href={site.cv} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Academic CV (PDF)</a>
            <a class="button-link" href={site.resume} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Résumé (PDF)</a>
            <a class="button-link button-link--quiet" href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>Email me</a>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
          <div class="section-heading"><h2>Selected work</h2></div>
          <div class="project-list">
            <article class="project-card">
              <h3>AutoSOUP</h3>
              <p class="project-card__meta">Purdue University, Duality Lab &middot; ACM CCS 2026 &middot; Presenting author</p>
              <p>
                A system that automates memory-safety verification of C components by generating unit proofs with
                LLMs and bounded model checking (CBMC). I co-develop it: I designed its debugging agent, which reads
                verification errors, diagnoses why a proof fails, and proposes a fix, and I built the cluster setup for
                its evaluation. Across 177 components from four embedded
                operating systems it verified 93% of candidate targets, exposed 66.7% of 60 known CVEs (versus 28.3%
                for a frontier coding agent), and uncovered 20 new vulnerabilities reported to maintainers.
              </p>
              <div class="project-card__links">
                <a href="/publication/autosoup/">CCS 2026 paper</a>
              </div>
            </article>
            <article class="project-card">
              <h3>FalseCrashReducer, in Google's OSS-Fuzz-Gen</h3>
              <p class="project-card__meta">With Google Open Source Security &middot; FSE 2026 (Industry)</p>
              <p>
                Two AI-driven strategies that cut false positive crashes in an industry-scale fuzz driver generation
                pipeline. Across 1,500 OSS-Fuzz benchmark functions they filtered out more than half of the crashes
                initially reported as program errors.
              </p>
              <div class="project-card__links">
                <a href="/publication/lessons-oss-fuzz-gen/">FSE 2026 paper</a>
                <a href="/publication/false-crash-reducer/">Extended preprint</a>
              </div>
            </article>
            <article class="project-card">
              <h3>EmNetTest</h3>
              <p class="project-card__meta">Purdue University &middot; ASE 2023 (21% acceptance)</p>
              <p>
                A systematic testing framework for embedded network stacks. With mentorship, I designed and implemented its
                fuzzing strategy and its evaluation, and contributed to the manual triage of results. It replicated 12 of 14 known IP/TCP/UDP vulnerabilities and discovered
                7 novel defects, 6 of which received CVEs, in stacks that prior fuzzing research had not broken.
              </p>
              <div class="project-card__links">
                <a href="/publication/emnettest/">ASE 2023 paper</a>
              </div>
            </article>
            <article class="project-card">
              <h3>How agents perform code optimization</h3>
              <p class="project-card__meta">Empirical study &middot; MSR 2026 (Mining Challenge)</p>
              <p>
                The first empirical comparison of agent- and human-authored performance optimization commits, over 324
                agent-generated and 83 human-authored pull requests. The extended study, which I co-first-authored,
                analyzes 1,130 agentic and 1,130 human-authored performance PRs: agentic PRs are merged less often
                (54.4% vs. 73.3%) and rely less on benchmarks, and about half of validated PRs report no quantitative
                performance metric.
              </p>
              <div class="project-card__links">
                <a href="/publication/code-optimization/">MSR 2026 paper</a>
                <a href="/publication/coding-agents-performance-validation/">Extended preprint</a>
              </div>
            </article>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
          <div class="section-heading"><h2>Technical skills</h2></div>
          <div class="skill-list">
            <div class="skill-row">
              <span class="skill-row__label">Research &amp; Security</span>
              <ul class="skill-row__items">
                <li>Formal verification</li>
                <li>Memory-safety verification</li>
                <li>Bounded model checking (CBMC)</li>
                <li>Program analysis</li>
                <li>Fuzzing</li>
                <li>Performance optimization</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="skill-row">
              <span class="skill-row__label">Programming</span>
              <ul class="skill-row__items">
                <li>C</li>
                <li>C++</li>
                <li>Python</li>
                <li>Java</li>
                <li>JavaScript</li>
                <li>TypeScript</li>
                <li>Dart</li>
                <li>SQL</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="skill-row">
              <span class="skill-row__label">AI for SE</span>
              <ul class="skill-row__items">
                <li>LLM agents</li>
                <li>Agentic pipelines</li>
                <li>Empirical evaluation</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="skill-row">
              <span class="skill-row__label">Engineering</span>
              <ul class="skill-row__items">
                <li>Spring Boot</li>
                <li>React</li>
                <li>Django</li>
                <li>Flask</li>
                <li>Flutter</li>
                <li>PostgreSQL</li>
                <li>Selenium</li>
                <li>Cucumber</li>
                <li>CI/CD</li>
                <li>Docker</li>
                <li>Linux</li>
                <li>Git</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
          <div class="section-heading"><h2>Education</h2></div>
          <ul class="home-list">
            <li><strong>PhD, Electrical and Computer Engineering</strong>, Purdue University (2025-2030 expected).</li>
            <li><strong>BSc, Systems and Computer Engineering</strong>, Universidad Nacional de Colombia (2018-2023), ranked #1 in Colombia; class rank 2/49.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
          <div class="section-heading"><h2>Research experience</h2></div>
          <ul class="home-list">
            <li><strong>Graduate Research Assistant</strong>, Purdue University (Aug 2025-present), co-developing AutoSOUP and designing its debugging agent.</li>
            <li><strong>Undergraduate Visiting Scholar (UREP-C)</strong>, Purdue University (Feb 2023-Jul 2023), where I designed and implemented EmNetTest's fuzzing strategy and evaluation.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
          <div class="section-heading"><h2>Teaching</h2></div>
          <ul class="home-list">
            <li><strong>Graduate Teaching Assistant</strong>, ECE 30861: Software Engineering, Purdue University (Fall 2026), grading assignments and holding office hours for about 150 students.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
          <div class="section-heading"><h2>Industry experience</h2></div>
          <ul class="home-list">
            <li><strong>Test Engineer and QA Analyst</strong>, Kravata (Sep 2024-Jul 2025), as the company's first and only QA engineer: I defined its testing strategy from scratch and automated unit, integration, and end-to-end tests in CI/CD.</li>
            <li><strong>Full-Stack Software Developer</strong>, Fit Ideas (Aug 2023-Aug 2024), leading a team of 4 developers on a white-label fuel sales app: architecture, code reviews, and Scrum.</li>
            <li><strong>Junior Software Developer</strong>, Fit Ideas (Aug 2021-Jan 2023), building web and mobile features, a configurable web scraper for public data, and relational databases.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
          <div class="section-heading"><h2>Academic service</h2></div>
          <ul class="home-list">
            <li>Reviewer for the <strong>MSR 2026 Mining Challenge Track</strong>.</li>
            <li>Sub-reviewer for <strong>ICSE 2026</strong>, <strong>ICSE 2027</strong>, and <strong>USENIX Security 2026 (Cycle 2)</strong>.</li>
            <li>Student volunteer at <strong>ICSE 2026</strong> in Rio de Janeiro, Brazil.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
          <div class="section-heading"><h2>Grants and scholarships</h2></div>
          <ul class="home-list">
            <li>Awarded the <a href="https://www.sigsac.org/ccs/CCS2026/attending/conference-grants.html"><strong>ACM CCS 2026 Student Conference Grant</strong></a> supporting conference registration and travel costs.</li>
            <li>Travel support for the <strong>ICSE 2026 Student Mentoring Workshop (SMeW)</strong> (NSF and ACM SIGSOFT).</li>
            <li><strong>Ser Pilo Paga</strong> merit scholarship (2017) from the Ministry of Education of Colombia, awarded for top national performance on the high-school exit examination; full undergraduate tuition.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <p class="home-closing">You can explore more in <a href="/publications/">Publications</a>, <a href="/talks/">Talks</a>, my <a href="/cv/">CV</a>, and my <a href={site.resume} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">résumé</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </ContentLayout>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
